MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Lead With Your Heart felt like a natural follow-up to The New Old Fashioned because vocal harmonies are what I want to hear now.",
    "To Be Loved and Andrea Bocelli - Amore also appealed through warm, melodic vocals, even though I would choose only the vocal-group album on this visit."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "25 and 19 took me toward pop, while What's Inside: Songs from Waitress suggested musical theater; neither matched my current interest in warm vocal harmonies.",
    "Wicked Game felt too dark for my current mood, and Traveller suggested a country direction I was not seeking. Precious Memories and Down To My Last Bad Habit gave me too little connection to my recent listening to invite a closer look."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The choices seemed to treat a broad interest in singing as enough, although solo pop, theatrical songs, and vocal-group harmonies are different listening experiences for me.",
    "A familiar or gentle vocal sound seemed to count too much when it did not also offer the group harmonies I wanted today."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My latest listen, The New Old Fashioned, mattered more to this visit than the older cluster of Christmas albums.",
    "The Christmas listening still suggested warmth and a seasonal interest, but it did not mean I would try any loosely related vocal album; on a brief visit, I needed a close match to choose even one."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my interest in warm vocals but stretched it too broadly beyond the vocal-group harmonies I wanted today."
}
